#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:111
#: 718d74db3e8845bf8da6078528ce6456
msgid "Setup Instructions for Example Tricks on a Switch Scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:113
#: b5e4774dbc9e43d08747aaf6e60b5221
msgid "Make sure you have Autotuned your plane and that its capable of doing aerobatics in ACRO mode well (Bixlers and flying wings only can do rolls and loops, generally....no yaw authority...ie should be able to knife edge for full capability). This includes Autotuning the new YAW rate controller. Enable :ref:`YAW_RATE_ENABLE<YAW_RATE_ENABLE>` and set :ref:`ACRO_YAW_RATE<ACRO_YAW_RATE>` appropriately (90deg/s is a good start). When you Autotune, not only do pitch and roll, but also yaw by exercising the rudder, like pitch and roll."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:114
#: 65f909f14d9a42f1bb5d45494f77efae
msgid "Enable scripting, on an autopilot that is capable (F7 or H7) with :ref:`SCR_ENABLE<SCR_ENABLE>` =1 and :ref:`SCR_HEAP_SIZE<SCR_HEAP_SIZE>` = 200000 (which will allow four trick scripts + AUTO mission scripting in the future)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:115
#: 5606c7034b7b433c96ec39ddf71b34fb
msgid "Copy the https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/examples/Aerobatics/Via_Switch scripts into your SD card APM/scripts directory. Use the RAW view and copy to files on the SD card using the same names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:116
#: 9b59af1a5c804882bd8a045fca88ba73
msgid "Assign an RC channel to ``RCx_OPTION`` = 300 for the trick activation switch (low=disable,mid=show trick number selected, high= do it) and one for 301 which is trick selection. You can use a three position for 0/5/10 trick id selection setup to ``RCx_OPTION`` = 301. 0 is disable, 5 is the knife edge, 10 is the loop/immelman example using the above scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:117
#: abe958537caf4ea7a27fa8bd6c0a12c3
msgid "Upon boot you should see messages that show the trick 5(knife-edge) and 10(loop/immelman) are loaded. Setting the activation switch to mid position will identify the trick number selected by the selection channel on the ground station or TX, if running :ref:`Yaapu <common-frsky-yaapu>` telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:118
#: a4f655283588405ca73f9c1715ee78d6
msgid "In the Ground Control Station's parameter lists, you should see a set of \"AERO\" params....the ``AERO_TRICK_RAT`` sets the loop pitch rate, try 90deg/s, ``AERO_RPT_COUNT`` sets the number of loops or if 0, an immelman. ``AERO_TRICK_ANG`` set the knife-edge trick angle 0 to 180 or -180 deg that will be executed as long as you have the activation switch high. Using the GCS or :ref:`Yaapu GCS<common-yaapu-gcs>` or :ref:`CRSF parameter editor<common-crsf-telemetry>`, you can change these in air to vary the trick characteristics, if you wish"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:119
#: 0d939f2c64304842a2ea005ee3f9a7f3
msgid "You can bail out of the trick by putting activation switch low, change modes, or set selector to 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-aerobatics.rst:121
#: 25db77cc35c74d4d8e6efb3ec7c5cfbf
msgid "Remember: ALTITUDE IS YOUR FRIEND! dont attempt your first one below 200feet! and FPV is a good way to try it out first, if you have trouble with seeing the vehicle at that altitude."
msgstr ""

